    <h1>Brown-necked Raven Range: Where This Species Lives</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="qa-snippet" aria-label="Direct answer">
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> The Brown-necked Raven (<em>Corvus ruficollis</em>) occupies the arid and semi-arid zones of North Africa (Sahara and sub-Saharan zone), the Middle East, Arabian Peninsula, Horn of Africa, and extending east through Iran and Afghanistan to Pakistan, India, and Central Asia. It is the raven of the Old World desert and steppe belt, essentially replacing the Common Raven in terrain too arid and hot for that species.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="qa-section">
    <h2>Distribution</h2>
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> The Brown-necked Raven's vast range spans desert and semi-desert zones:<sup><a href="#src-1">1</a></sup></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Atlantic Islands:</strong> Cape Verde Islands; Canary Islands (Lanzarote, Fuerteventura — where it overlaps with Common Raven).</li>
      <li><strong>North Africa:</strong> throughout the Sahara from Morocco and Mauritania east to Egypt and Sudan. Also the sub-Saharan Sahel zone (Mali, Niger, Chad, Sudan) in arid shrubland.</li>
      <li><strong>East Africa:</strong> the arid lowlands of Somalia, Djibouti, Eritrea, and eastern Ethiopia (below the highlands, where the Thick-billed Raven occupies the equivalent highland niche).</li>
      <li><strong>Middle East:</strong> throughout — Sinai, Israel (Negev), Jordan, Syria, Iraq, Kuwait, Saudi Arabia, Yemen, Oman, UAE.</li>
      <li><strong>Iran, Afghanistan, Pakistan:</strong> throughout the arid interior plateau zones.</li>
      <li><strong>India:</strong> restricted to the most arid areas — Rajasthan (Thar Desert), Gujarat (Kutch), and Sindh (Pakistan). Easternmost regular occurrence.</li>
      <li><strong>Central Asia:</strong> Turkmenistan, Uzbekistan, Tajikistan, and adjacent steppe/desert zones.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="qa-section">
    <h2>Habitat</h2>
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> Within its range, the Brown-necked Raven occupies arid and semi-arid open habitats:<sup><a href="#src-1">1</a></sup></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Primary:</strong> true desert (erg, reg, hammada), semi-desert and steppe with scattered shrubs (Saharan halophytes, Acacia-Commiphora scrub), wadis (dry riverbeds) with cliff faces for nesting.</li>
      <li><strong>Secondary:</strong> oases, date palm plantations, agricultural land in arid zones, and human settlements — where food subsidies allow penetration into otherwise unsuitable terrain.</li>
      <li><strong>Tolerance:</strong> one of the most heat- and aridity-tolerant corvids, capable of living in terrain with rainfall below 50 mm/year.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

